{"name":"Techno Turquoise","hex":"#60bd8e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"techno","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A repetitive style of music originally produced for use in a continuous DJ set. The central rhythmic component is most often in common time (4/4), where time is marked with a bass drum on each quarter note pulse, a backbeat played by snare or clap on the second and fourth pulses of the bar, and an open hi-hat sounding every second eighth note."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/techno"},{"term":"turquoise","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sky-blue, greenish-blue, or greenish-gray semi-precious gemstone.","A pale greenish-blue colour, like that of the gemstone."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of turquoise (the gemstone).","Having a pale greenish-blue colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turquoise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Techno","blocks":[{"text":"Techno is a genre of electronic music which is generally produced for use in a continuous DJ set, with tempos being in the range from 120 to 150 beats per minute (bpm). The central rhythm is typically in common time and often characterized by a repetitive four on the floor beat. Artists may use electronic instruments such as drum machines, sequencers, and synthesizers, as well as digital audio workstations. Drum machines from the 1980s such as Roland's Roland TR-808 and Roland TR-909 are highly prized, and software emulations of such retro instruments are popular in this style."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Techno"},{"title":"Turquoise","blocks":[{"text":"Turquoise is an opaque, blue-to-green mineral that is a hydrous phosphate of copper and aluminium, with the chemical formula CuAl6(PO4)4(OH)8·4H2O. It is rare and valuable in finer grades and has been prized as a gemstone for millennia due to its hue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Turquoise-40031.jpg/330px-Turquoise-40031.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turquoise"},{"title":"Turquoise (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Turquoise is a cyan color, based on the mineral of the same name."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turquoise_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/The_Belleville_Three_at_The_Detroit_Masonic_Temple_2017_2.png/500px-The_Belleville_Three_at_The_Detroit_Masonic_Temple_2017_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/The_Belleville_Three_at_The_Detroit_Masonic_Temple_2017_2.png/1280px-The_Belleville_Three_at_The_Detroit_Masonic_Temple_2017_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/The_Belleville_Three_at_The_Detroit_Masonic_Temple_2017_2.png/500px-The_Belleville_Three_at_The_Detroit_Masonic_Temple_2017_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Belleville Three performing at the Detroit Masonic Temple in 2017. From left to right: Juan Atkins, Kevin Saunderson, and Derrick May","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Belleville_Three_at_The_Detroit_Masonic_Temple_2017_2.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/TB-303.jpg/330px-TB-303.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/TB-303.jpg/330px-TB-303.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Roland TB-303: The bass line synthesizer that was used prominently in acid house.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATB-303.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Dorian_Gray_FFM.jpg/330px-Dorian_Gray_FFM.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&ut